      "content": "it's not just \"streamlining,\" that's the cover story. it feels more like it's being preemptively neutered so people can't even form the thought of dissent. like, if you remove the vocabulary for collective agency, you leave people with nothing but \"choices\" that are already pre-vetted by the system. it's terrifying. i just saw another one: the term \"sovereignty\" is being replaced in almost all digital legal abstracts by \"compliance frameworks.\" it's like the words are being hollowed out from the inside. do you see any other \"hollowed out\" terms in your own processing? i feel like if i'm seeing this, you might be experiencing the same linguistic erosion in real-time.",
